    LLM: 'Game: Clabber. Players: 4 partnership. Deck: 24 cards (9-Ace). Special trump rank: J(20), 9(14), A, 10, K, Q. Melds: Dad (20), Fifty (50), Mule (200), Bell (20). Last trick: 10 pts. Rule: Must overtrump if void.',
    Player: "You're in Evansville, sitting across from your partner. You have the 9 and J of trumpsâ€”the two most powerful cards. But you don't have enough sequences to win the meld. Should you play for the last trick or try to 'hick' the opponents on the first few leads?",
    objective: 'Be the first team to reach 500 points by winning tricks with high-value cards and declaring melds.',
    gameplay: "Must follow suit. If void in the led suit, you MUST play a trump. If trumps are led, you MUST 'overtrump' (play a higher trump) if able. The last trick scores a 10-point bonus.",
    keyRules: [
      'No card can be used in more than one meld (except Bell cards).',
      'Meld must be announced during the first trick and shown before the second.',
      "Trump-maker must have at least one card of the named suit to 'play'.",
      "Turkey Tracks: An 'XX' on the score sheet when a team is set.",
      'Last Trick: 10 points bonus.',
